If a patient has a severe-acute-pain and receives a benzodiazepine during a long-term-therapy and the benzodiazepine has a stable-low-dosage then an opioid-prescription possibly can be appropriate for the patient.
If a clinician prescribes an opioid-pain-medication with a benzodiazepine then the clinician should particularly prescribe the opioid-pain-medication with the benzodiazepine cautiously.
